        ('They talk to Grimsby', '“Hm.” He does not look up. If they persist: “You have twenty minutes to eat. I suggest you use them.”'),
        ('They talk to the Headmaster', 'His welcome line. He asks how they are settling in and seems to really want to know.'),
        ('Cassius picks on someone', 'He flicks a pea at the Quill, or says the Marlowe’s name loudly. A teacher is watching: if they retaliate with magic, −5 points.'),
        ('They search the Great Hall', 'Under the tables: chewing gum from 1890. Behind the staff table: a door to a small chamber where the staff meet. It is locked. Through the keyhole, a painting of a sunlit garden that Ashgrove hung last week.'),
