    ('read', 'The dungeons are cold enough to see your breath. Jars line the walls: things floating in green liquid, things that might once have had eyes. Professor Grimsby does not look up when you come in.'),
    ('say', 'Professor Grimsby', '“Sit. Open your books. If anyone’s cauldron explodes, they clean it up themselves.”'),
    ('gm', 'Start the class minigame (Stir Timing). Passing gives two Pepperup Potions and 10 XP.'),
    ('ifs', [
        ('Someone does well', 'Grimsby looks at the cauldron for a long moment. “Adequate.” From him, that is a medal. +5 points if they deserve it.'),
        ('Someone’s cauldron explodes', 'Spin Potion brewing for what it does. They clean it up themselves, as promised.'),
        ('They read the jars', 'Most are ingredients. One is labelled “Boomslang skin” and is nearly empty. Another, “Lacewing flies”, is empty. Grimsby has not noticed yet.'),
        ('They ask Grimsby a question', '“Hm.” If it is a good question about potions, he answers it properly, and seems annoyed that he enjoyed it.'),
    ]),

    ('h2', 'Day 1, Free time'),
    where([['The Dungeons', 'Grimsby (furious)'], ['Grand Staircase', 'Peeves, the ghost, Prefect Sinclair'], ['The Courtyard', 'Cassius'],
           ['Trophy Room', 'Filch'], ['Forbidden Forest', 'the centaur'], ['Elsewhere', 'Professors in their rooms, Pip, the librarian, the matron']]),
    ('p', '<b>Appears:</b> the stolen ingredient jars, hidden on the Grand Staircase.'),
    ('read', 'A crash echoes from the dungeons, then a voice you already recognise, very loud: “WHO HAS BEEN IN MY CUPBOARD?” Students scatter. Professor Grimsby storms up the corridor with his robes flapping, glaring at every first-year he passes.'),
    ('say', 'Professor Grimsby', '“Somebody has been in my store cupboard. Boomslang skin. Lacewing flies. Gone. If I find out it was a first-year, they will be scrubbing cauldrons until they are forty.”'),
    ('gm', 'Give Stolen Ingredients to anyone who offers to help. Pin “Grimsby’s store cupboard was raided” under Grimsby when they look at the cupboard.'),
    ('p', 'This is the first big free block. Here is everything they can do:'),
    ('ifs', [
        ('They search the store cupboard', 'INT 12: sticky fingerprints, too big for a student and slightly see-through. A trail of lacewing wings leads up the stairs. (It is Peeves.)'),
        ('They follow the trail to the Grand Staircase', 'Peeves is there, juggling. The jars are on a landing above. To get them: corner Peeves (DEX or CHA 13), or Wingardium Leviosa, or climb a moving staircase (DEX 12, a fall is 2 HP).'),
        ('They meet Prefect Sinclair at the staircase', 'Keep an Eye Out, step 1. She is early and nervous. She says she will show them the bad corridor tonight, after curfew.'),
        ('They go to the Library', 'The first rune tablet is on a reading desk (pick it up from the Here tab). The Locked chest is by the windows. The librarian watches.'),
        ('The Fenwick studies the map', 'Put The Torn Edge on the TV. It is a lovely first puzzle and teaches the first runes.'),
        ('They visit the Trophy Room', 'Filch is polishing. The Scratched note (first ring clue) is tucked behind a cup. A WIS 12 notices it before he does.'),
        ('They climb to the Owlery or the Astronomy Tower', 'A ring clue in each, and a chest. Nothing in the clues makes sense yet. That is fine.'),
        ('They find the Kitchens', 'Tickle the pear. Pip feeds them. The Small chest is by the ovens.'),
        ('They go to the Forest', 'Out of bounds. The centaur is there, speaking to the sky. Spin the Forest wheel.'),
    ]),
    ('tip', 'Day 1 Free time is the best moment to show them how big the world is. If they only do the quest, describe what they pass on the way: an owl with a parcel too heavy for it, a ghost crying in a corridor, a portrait of a knight challenging them to a duel.'),

    ('h2', 'Day 1, Curfew'),
    where([['Grand Staircase', 'Filch, Peeves, Prefect Sinclair (patrolling)'], ['The Library', 'the ghost'],
           ['Forbidden Forest', 'the centaur'], ['Elsewhere', 'Pip in the Kitchens, the matron']]),
    ('p', '<b>Appears:</b> a swarm of Cornish Pixies on the Grand Staircase (they leave when the block ends).'),
    ('gm', 'Anyone who moves around spins Out after curfew. A group that meets the prefect can travel with her, and Filch will not spin for them while she is there.'),
    ('h3', 'Keep an Eye Out: the patrol'),
    ('read', 'Prefect Sinclair is waiting at the foot of the Grand Staircase, wand lit, pretending she isn’t nervous. “Quietly,” she whispers. She leads you down a corridor you have never seen. Every frame on the walls is empty. Painted chairs, painted gardens, painted skies, and nobody in any of them.'),
    ('say', 'Prefect Sinclair', '“They were all here last week. All of them. Now look.” She stops at a dead end where the air is so cold your breath clouds. “That’s where it’s worst. Under there, somewhere.”'),
    ('ifs', [
        ('They tap the wall at the dead end', 'It is cold, colder than stone should be. A WIS 14: faintly, from below, something humming.'),
        ('The Okafor touches the wall', 'A curse, deep down, enormous and old. Like putting a hand on a sleeping animal.'),
        ('The Pixies attack on the staircase', 'Four HP each, fast, annoying. They steal one small item each if not stopped. Good first fight. If Filch hears the fight: Out after curfew for everyone.'),
        ('They sneak to the Kitchens', 'Pip is delighted. Midnight snacks. No danger at all.'),
    ]),
    ('h3', 'The beat'),
    ('read', 'Late that night, two figures carry something large and wrapped down a stairway that most students do not know exists. They hang it in a dead-end corridor deep under the castle. When they leave, the corridor is very, very quiet. Then the cloth stirs, though there is no wind.'),
    ('p', 'Read this to the whole table, as a cutaway. Then, privately, to the Quill: they wake with a jolt from a dream of a painted eye.'),

